# rule.forbid.redundant-expensive-operations

never call the same expensive operation (api, db, network, >10ms, paid) in adjacent then blocks, and never share an async result via `let`. each repeat wastes time + money and adds flake

cure — call once with test-fns `useThen`, share the result:
```ts
when('[t0] operation is executed', () => {
  const result = useThen('it succeeds', async () => expensiveOperation({ input }));
  then('returns output', () => { expect(result.output).toBeDefined(); });
  then('returns cost', () => { expect(result.cost.total).toBeDefined(); });
});
```
across when blocks (idempotency, before/after): `useWhen` (rule.require.useThen-useWhen-for-shared-results)

enforcement: redundant expensive operation in adjacent then blocks = blocker; `let` declared to share an async result = blocker
